# Push Notifications, Android Apps, Egress & Security

This project ships two Capacitor Android apps built from this repo plus push notifications via FCM. Keep this architecture in mind for every change.

## Android apps
- Technician app: `android/` (package `com.hydrogenro.technician`, APK `HRO-Technician-debug.apk`)
- Admin app: `android-admin/` (package `com.hydrogenro.admin`, APK `HRO-Admin-debug.apk`)
- Both use notification channel `job_alerts_v2` with custom sounds (`res/raw/tech_alert.wav` / `admin_chime.wav`), created natively in `NotificationChannels.java`. Never create this channel from JS (old APKs lack the sound file and would lock it silent).
- Web-layer changes reach phones via Netlify deploy; native (Java/gradle/res) changes require a new APK.

## Push notifications (FCM, free tier)
- Firebase service account lives in the `app_secrets` table (key `firebase_service_account`), NOT env vars (4KB Lambda env limit).
- Shared sender helper: `netlify/functions/fcm-helper.js` (`getMessaging`, `sendToTechnicianDevices`, token pruning).
- Admin devices: `admin_push_tokens` table (multi-device). Technician devices: `technician_push_tokens` table (multi-device, one row per device, registered via `register_technician_push_token` RPC) with legacy fallback `technician_live_locations.fcm_token`.
- All technician-facing senders fan out to every logged-in device and prune tokens FCM reports dead. Logout deletes that device's token.
- Scheduled functions (netlify.toml cron, IST times): daily-cash-check 9:00 PM, daily-expense-review 9:15 PM (tech + business expenses Yes/No → Payments), morning-cash-reminder 8:30 AM (techs admin marked unpaid), evening-summary 10:00 PM, parts-reminder 10:10 PM (techs who completed jobs + all admins), admin-reminders-push 9:00 AM.

## Standing requirements for ALL new work

Keep these forever unless the user explicitly relaxes them:

### Security
- Every new table: **RLS** (`public.is_admin_user()` for admin, `auth.uid()` for own rows).
- **SECURITY DEFINER** RPCs only when RLS cannot express the rule; lock `search_path` and validate inputs.
- Service-role keys / Meta tokens / Firebase / R2 secrets: **server-side only** (Netlify functions / scripts). Never expose to the client.
- Prefer signed short-lived URLs for private media (R2); no long-lived public buckets for chat media when avoidable.

### Minimize Supabase egress
- Select **only needed columns**; no `select('*')` on hot paths.
- **No polling** in production CRM — Realtime, fetch-on-open, or user action.
- Reuse already-fetched data; patch local state on send/realtime instead of full reloads.
- Prefer one RPC / upsert over N round-trips.
- Cache list/thread summaries in **memory + sessionStorage** (TTL) where safe; soft-refresh instead of hard reload.
- Page messages (newest-first); load older on scroll; soft refresh must **merge**, never wipe scrolled history.
- Heavy files live on **Cloudflare R2** (egress bandwidth free); don’t store PDF/image bytes in Supabase rows.

### Minimize Netlify / server function invocations
- Don’t call a function from the client on every keystroke, scroll tick, or mount if cache/Realtime can serve.
- Batch or debounce outbound sends / signed-URL fetches; reuse resolved media URLs in-memory for the session.
- Avoid “refresh everything” after tiny actions — update the one row/thread locally.
- Cron/scheduled work: keep payloads slim; don’t re-fetch full tables when a targeted query works.

### Prefer local memory over the network
- Open inbox / reopen chat: show cache first, network only if stale or missing.
- After user loads older pages, keep them in the open-chat state/cache until leave/cap — don’t discard via soft cap bugs.
- Optional later (IndexedDB, APK local DB) is fine; until then session + memory cache is the default.
